**Example Script - HTML Form and Server Interaction**

```javascript
// HTML form (to gather user data)
<form id="myForm">
  <input type="text" name="name" placeholder="Your Name">
  <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your Email">
  <input type="submit" value="Submit">
</form>

// JavaScript to handle form submission
const form = document.getElementById('myForm');
form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
  event.preventDefault(); // Prevent the default form submission

  // Capture user input from form fields
  const name = document.getElementsByName('name')[0].value;
  const email = document.getElementsByName('email')[0].value;

  // (Here, you would send this data to a server for processing)

  // Display a message to the user 
  alert(`Name: ${name}\nEmail: ${email}`);
});
```


**Explanation:**

* **HTML Form:** The script uses an HTML form to collect user input. 
* **Event Listener:**  An event listener is attached to the form for when it is submitted.
* **`preventDefault()`:** Prevents the form from actually reloading the page, which could have been the initial behavior.
* **Data Capture:** The script extracts data from the input fields.
* **Data Processing:**  In a real application, this data would be sent to a server for storage or further processing.

**Important Note:**  It is crucial to have a robust security model in place and follow best practices to protect user data. 


